  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 238 PM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nConditions are expected to remain warm on Tuesday, and much like the \nprevious days, expecting warmest conditions will remain along and \nwest of Highway 83, with highs pushing into the mid to upper 90s. \nWill also be keeping an eye out for potential elevated fire weather \nconcerns west of Highway 61 again, as humidity drops around 25 \npercent in the afternoon with gusty easterly winds, up to 25 mph. \n\nBy mid week, guidance suggests an upper level trough attempts to \ntrack over the western United States, slightly pushing the ridge to \nthe west. This signal continues to be noted with the latest forecast \ncycles, continuing to build confidence in the pattern shift. \nHowever, there is still a bit of uncertainty in the amplitude of the \nvarious upper level features, so there may still be some slight \nrefinement on timing over the next few forecast cycles as guidance \ncomes into consensus. Regardless, this is expected to usher in a \nmore active upper level pattern, increasing chances of precipitation \nWednesday onward. Ensemble guidance suggests fairly strong chances \nfor at least measureable precipitation, with the European ensembles \nremaining more optimistic than the GEFS solutions on precipitation \nchances and amounts. Along with the increasing precipitation \npotential, expecting to see a cooling pattern by mid week as well. \nIn fact, this trend continues to suggest highs that may be around 10 \nto 15 degrees below average to end the week, with highs dropping \ninto the 70s.",
